.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES CDFMC-MANAGED-FTD ONBOARD" "1" "2026-08-18" "0.39.1" "sccfm-cli inventory devices cdfmc-managed-ftd onboard Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-cdfmc-managed-ftd\-onboard \- Onboard a cdFMC-managed FTD device (non-ZTP).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices cdfmc-managed-ftd onboard
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Onboard a cdFMC-managed FTD device (non-ZTP).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name TEXT
Human-readable name for the FTD device.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-fmc\-access\-policy\-uid\fP TEXT
UUID of the FMC access policy to apply to this device.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-licenses\fP [BASE|CARRIER|THREAT|MALWARE|URLFilter]
License(s) to apply to the device. Can be specified multiple times (e.g. --licenses BASE --licenses CARRIER).  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-virtual\fP
Indicate that the FTD is a virtual device. Requires --performance-tier.
.TP
\fB\-\-performance\-tier\fP [FTDv5|FTDv10|FTDv20|FTDv30|FTDv50|FTDv100|FTDv]
Performance tier of the FTDv (required when --virtual is set, e.g., FTDv5, FTDv10, FTDv20).
.TP
\fB\-\-grouped\-labels\fP TEXT
Grouped labels in JSON format, e.g., '{"environment": ["prod", "us-west"]}'.
.TP
\fB\-\-ungrouped\-labels\fP TEXT
Free-form labels to assign to the device (can be specified multiple times).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without onboarding.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
